{
  "an9.11:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.11 ",
  "an9.11:0.2": "2. The Lion’s Roar ",
  "an9.11:0.3": "Sāriputta’s Lion’s Roar ",
  "an9.11:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an9.11:1.2": "Then Venerable Sāriputta went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "an9.11:1.3": "“Sir, I have completed the rainy season residence at Sāvatthī. ",
  "an9.11:1.4": "I wish to leave to wander the countryside.” ",
  "an9.11:1.5": "“Please, Sāriputta, go at your convenience.” ",
  "an9.11:1.6": "Then Sāriputta rose from his seat, bowed, and respectfully circled the Buddha, keeping him on his right, before leaving. ",
  "an9.11:1.7": "And then, not long after Sāriputta had left, a certain monk said to the Buddha, ",
  "an9.11:1.8": "“Sir, Venerable Sāriputta attacked me and left without saying sorry.” ",
  "an9.11:1.9": "So the Buddha addressed one of the monks, ",
  "an9.11:1.10": "“Please, monk, in my name tell Sāriputta that ",
  "an9.11:1.11": "the Teacher summons him.” ",
  "an9.11:1.12": "“Yes, sir,” that monk replied. He went to Sāriputta and said to him, ",
  "an9.11:1.13": "“Reverend Sāriputta, the Teacher summons you.” ",
  "an9.11:1.14": "“Yes, reverend,” Sāriputta replied. ",
  "an9.11:2.1": "Now at that time the venerables Mahāmoggallāna and Ānanda, taking a latchkey, went from dwelling to dwelling, saying: ",
  "an9.11:2.2": "“Come forth, venerables! Com